A||||3||kslish||Carlisle All-GM Nationals, any interest?||||1||
Z||000000||kslish||04-05-2001||06:50 PM||||I posting this to guage interest in a Fiero gathering at the All-GM Nationals in Carlisle the weekend of June 29th-July 1, 2001.  This is the first year for the All-GM show at Carlisle.<P>Do you think that many Fiero owners would be willing to attend do to the fact that it is only about 6 weeks after MAFOA's Fieros at Carlisle (which is May 19th)?  <P>I'm just thinking that a Fiero showing at a big GM show may attract some positive attention to the Fiero, and I think it only takes 20 cars pre-registered under the same model to get a area partitioned off and a tent provided free of charge.  <P>More details on the show can be found at: <A HREF="http://www.carlisleproductions.com/gm2001/gm_home.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carlisleproductions.com/gm2001/gm_home.htm</A> <P>Does this date conflict with any other Fiero events?  Any other input on the idea?<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-05-2001||07:00 PM||||1 carlisle event is enough for my fix per year. I go to cruises/shows almost every weekend. Anyone here going to Sharonville (north Cincinatti) Apr 29. Just a very big car show, not Fiero. They close downtown, last year there was prob close to 1,000 cars.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||04-06-2001||12:40 AM||||Yeah, I plan on going to the All GM nats in carlisle.  I will probably be bringing some friends of mine and their Fiero's too.  Would be cool to have an area just for the Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">       <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif">  <BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/3dlil/eek2.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||grgoyl86||04-06-2001||07:07 PM||||MAFOA is planning to have a gathering at the All-GM Nationals. We aren't planning any of our own trophies, just getting a place for all the Fieros to hang out together and compare notes. We hope to see a lot of you there!<BR>Watch our website (www.fieropride.com) for more details.<P>Bob Schlag||||reg||10
